WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:05.899
Donald Trump's Senate impeachment trial is
underway, sort of, but not really.

00:00:05.899 --> 00:00:06.899
We actually

00:00:06.899 --> 00:00:14.270
dreamed hours and hours of yesterday's proceedings,
which went into the night and it was in a

00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:18.140
sense the start of Donald Trump's impeachment
trial.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:23.900
But I say not really because it was filled
merely with amendment proposals and debates

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:31.429
and subsequent tabling by Republicans of those
amendments by Democrats all about how is impeachment

00:00:31.429 --> 00:00:32.439
going to be done.

00:00:32.439 --> 00:00:36.941
And one of the big arguments was over to catch
you up, like if you missed everything, if

00:00:36.941 --> 00:00:40.149
you missed what, what was it, eight hours,
I don't know how long it went yesterday.

00:00:40.149 --> 00:00:43.609
If you missed all of those hours, you really
didn't miss very much.

00:00:43.609 --> 00:00:49.420
It was one of the big arguments was Republicans
want to deal with documents and witnesses

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:54.170
after both sides have had 24 hours each to
make their arguments.

00:00:54.170 --> 00:01:00.620
And after the a hundred senators have had
16 hours to ask questions of the prosecutors

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:05.869
and the defenders, this would be like in a
criminal trial saying documents it would and

00:01:05.869 --> 00:01:06.869
witnesses?

00:01:06.869 --> 00:01:07.869
No, no, no.

00:01:07.869 --> 00:01:10.720
First we want both sides to make all of their
arguments.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:14.200
We'll give the jury a chance to deliberate
and come back with questions if they have

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.200
any.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:19.729
And then after all of that is done, we'll
discuss whether any witnesses are going to

00:01:19.729 --> 00:01:23.930
testify, including witnesses to the alleged
crimes that are being adjudicated here.

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:25.619
It's a laughing stock, it's a farce.

00:01:25.619 --> 00:01:28.600
It's a joke of a trial if you do it that way.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:35.899
So Democrats ended up in the impossible position
of having to propose amendments to deal with

00:01:35.899 --> 00:01:42.450
at least the document piece now or of sitting
back and allowing Republicans to just say

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:47.740
we're going to deal with documents and witnesses
later and implicitly saying that that's okay

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.930
by not putting forth amendments to try to
change that.

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:55.650
So Democrats proposed an amendment to subpoena
documents from the white house.

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:59.250
Now they debated that amendment nearly two
hours.

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:04.130
And then of course Republicans have a majority
Republicans voted to table or put off that

00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:10.479
decision with a 53 to 47 party line vote saying
we'll deal with documents after the trial.

00:02:10.479 --> 00:02:14.620
So then Chuck Schumer stands up the Senate
minority leader and proposes another amendment

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:17.230
this time to subpoena documents from the state
department.

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:18.930
And of course the exact same results.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:24.640
53 to 47 Republicans say, we already have
a process of marble, marble mouth.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:29.209
Mitch McConnell stood up and says, we're going
to be dealing with documents and witnesses

00:02:29.209 --> 00:02:35.970
after 48 and 1664 hours of, uh, of, of testimony,
our arguments and questions we'll deal with

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:36.970
later.

00:02:36.970 --> 00:02:39.510
53 to 47 Republicans table it.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:42.140
So then Democrats say, we have an amendment.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:45.980
We want to subpoena chief of staff, Mick Mulvaney
or no.

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:47.849
Next was a documents from the OMB.

00:02:47.849 --> 00:02:51.650
And then we want to subpoena Mick Mulvaney.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:54.440
Then we want to subpoena the documents from
the defense department.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.480
We want to subpoena Robert Blair Mulvaney.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.090
He's a senior advisor.

00:02:58.090 --> 00:03:00.360
We want to subpoena Michael Duffy.

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:03.560
The OMB is associate director for national
security.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:06.330
We want to subpoena national security advisor,
John Bolton.

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:07.750
We'll talk about that later.

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:12.830
And of course, Democrats can't win those amendments
because they don't have the votes, but they

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:18.159
can't just stay silent about this atrocity
being committed by Republicans led by Senate

00:03:18.159 --> 00:03:20.030
majority leader Mitch McConnell.

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:26.110
So they have to do the logical and obvious
thing, which is we don't agree with the process.

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:32.930
We don't agree with 64 hours of proceedings
before we debate which documents and witnesses

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:34.140
will be admitted.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:37.370
So they have no choice but to introduce these
amendments.

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:42.080
Every single one of which was of course tabled
by Republicans.

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:47.939
Eventually senators approved a roadmap for
impeachment for the trial, which Mitch McConnell

00:03:47.939 --> 00:03:48.939
laid out.

00:03:48.939 --> 00:03:53.890
And again, Democrats don't have the numbers,
but the important parameters are that each

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:57.500
side will have 24 hours to present opening
arguments.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:02.090
Mitch McConnell wanted each side to have two
days for those 24 hours.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:04.439
That's 12 hours a day.

00:04:04.439 --> 00:04:10.400
That is a Republican strategy to have insanely
late night stuff going on, which way fewer

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.010
people would see.

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:17.620
They were able to get Republicans to say,
okay, we can spread the 24 hours over three

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:20.150
days, meaning it won't go as late into the
night.

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:26.290
Uh, any, uh, uh, uh, another sort of compromise
is that subpoenas for witnesses and documents

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:28.890
will be debated after opening arguments.

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:31.350
So understand the insanity of this.

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:37.910
What Republicans wanted was to have 24 hours
of opening arguments from one side, 24 hours

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:44.100
of opening arguments from the other side and
16 hours of questions from senators and then

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:48.100
to debate subpoenas and witnesses, subpoenas
of documents and witnesses.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:51.190
What they've Democrats want it to do it right
now, which makes sense.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:55.970
What they've agreed upon is they will do the
48 hours of opening arguments.

00:04:55.970 --> 00:05:02.450
Then debate subpoenaing documents and witnesses,
a small concession but a concession nonetheless

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:07.170
and then all of the house evidence, the stuff
that came up during the intelligence and the

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:14.320
judiciary hearings, that will all be automatically
part of the Senate trial unless someone objects

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:21.150
rather than having to introduce bits of evidence
and testimony piece by piece.

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:22.150
Okay.

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:25.010
Only water and milk were allowed into the
Senate chamber.

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:29.780
There was a rule of silence during yesterday's
proceedings which led to senators flashing

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:36.280
almost like flashcards, flashing pieces of
paper with notes on them to other crazy.

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:37.280
So today is day two.

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:40.560
I hope you'll again join me for a live stream
on YouTube and Twitch.

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:43.960
Yesterday's live stream saw nearly a hundred
thousand different people.

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:46.810
Join us over the course of the afternoon and
evening.

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:48.640
We'll be back at it today.

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:50.540
Here's what to watch for today.

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:54.490
Do Donald Trump's lawyers respond with any
substance?

00:05:54.490 --> 00:06:00.160
Yesterday, Adam Schiff and the other democratic
impeachment managers, uh, we're talking about

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:05.960
substance and meanwhile, Trump's lawyers,
Pat sip, Aloni and Jay Sekulow talked about

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:06.960
circumstances.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:11.600
They talked about, we weren't invited to things
that they actually were invited to.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:13.130
They talked about Joe Biden.

00:06:13.130 --> 00:06:17.200
They talked about everything other than the
actual substance of the allegations.

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:19.680
So question one for today is, will they talk
about substance?

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:21.470
I predict no.

00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:25.770
Number two today, there's going to be a whole
new round of motions, including more than

00:06:25.770 --> 00:06:31.410
likely motions by Republicans to dismiss the
entire case against Donald Trump.

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:36.120
Trump wildly suggested that the entire impeachment
trial should simply be canceled on Twitter

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:37.430
a couple of weeks ago.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:40.590
And we know that when Donald Trump says jump
Republicans say how high?

00:06:40.590 --> 00:06:42.560
And that is likely something they will do
today.

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:45.350
Argue the entire case should just be canceled.

00:06:45.350 --> 00:06:50.270
By the time you hear this segment or watch
today's show, we will likely know whether

00:06:50.270 --> 00:06:54.720
they've submitted such motions because they're
doing writing before they actually start.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:58.190
If you are wondering, this seems like a lot
of sidebar.

00:06:58.190 --> 00:07:02.780
When will the actual substantive arguments
begin?

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:03.780
We don't know.

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:04.780
It could happen later this week.

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:05.920
Friday could be Saturday.

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:07.980
They do plan to go six days a week.

00:07:07.980 --> 00:07:12.020
The substance may not even start until early
next week.

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:13.770
It's going to be very long.

00:07:13.770 --> 00:07:18.770
Donald Trump will be acquitted at the end
unless something completely beyond our ability

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:22.930
to predict happens and the most important
message is this one.

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:30.040
Yesterday you had people on both sides, Democrats
and Donald Trump's lawyers arguing that if

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:33.200
this is not a full and fair trial, it's not
good for anyone.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:37.710
In other words, the argument was if people
don't believe, if the public doesn't believe

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:42.340
that this is a fair trial, an acquittal isn't
very powerful and a conviction isn't very

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:43.340
powerful.

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:44.560
They are wrong.

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:51.130
Given that an acquittal is all but a foregone
conclusion, only half the country really cares

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:52.610
about a fair trial.

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:53.980
This won't be a fair trial.

00:07:53.980 --> 00:07:55.450
There may or may not be witnesses.

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:59.250
It will be a sham in which Republicans have
already prejudged and we know they will vote

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:04.220
to acquit, but Trumpus would be fine with
that when they say, unless this is a full

00:08:04.220 --> 00:08:05.240
and fair trial.

00:08:05.240 --> 00:08:09.910
And acquittal of Donald Trump isn't worth
very much wrong, Trump is, we'll see the eventual

00:08:09.910 --> 00:08:12.600
acquittal as an exoneration.

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:15.790
And then they will say, look, Trump did nothing
wrong.

00:08:15.790 --> 00:08:17.060
He was exonerated.

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:21.470
So where I completely disagree with what has
been argued from both sides.

00:08:21.470 --> 00:08:26.610
Adam Schiff argued this and also Trump's lawyers
argued this, Trump doesn't need a fair trial

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:28.330
for his acquittal to be accepted.

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:33.950
His followers will accept the acquittal as
an exoneration, no matter what kind of a kangaroo

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:36.760
court ends up rendering that verdict.

00:08:36.760 --> 00:08:37.760
Let's now focus in on one witness.

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:37.763
Uh, John Bolton.

